From b3782cfb74b5d3e4af461772038a64e06b355415 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: RTSP-on-GE design <rtsp-on-ge@example.invalid>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 19:39:38 -0500
Subject: [PATCH alpha 4/4] winedmo, mfmediaengine: stabilize asynchronous
 media loading and VOD control

Keep URLMon HTTP compatibility as a full-cache fallback, but move its blocking open to an MF I/O work item and preserve the cached stream length and position. Direct HLS remains on FFmpeg instead of redundantly fetching a manifest through URLMon. This does not claim incremental HTTP playback.

Make source loading generation-aware and detach old presentations before lock-dropping shutdown. Preserve current play intent across asynchronous completion, discard stale results safely, and shut down live presentation state before releasing the media session.

Use per-stream FIFO sample tokens with one logical worker, request generations, demux seek epochs, bounded queues, and one-shot EOS/EOP. Keep every active A/V stream primed before shared backpressure stops demuxing, so a full video queue cannot starve an empty audio queue.

Coalesce running SetCurrentTimeEx updates, preserve GE synchronization suppression, and schedule one guaranteed final seek after 250 ms of quiet. Paused seeks remain immediate and scheduling failure falls back to a synchronous flush.

Correct demux stream-index mapping, own late asynchronous read buffers, guard simple-buffer allocation overflow, use the MediaSource seek capability flag, propagate seek failures, and harden custom AVIO seek arithmetic, HLS deadlines, timestamp conversion, and teardown ordering.
